                                RESTRICTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. NO COPYING
     Unauthorized copying of any content is strictly prohibited, regardless
     of the source of inspiration for that content. This includes partial
     copies, adaptations, and translations into other programming languages.

  2. NO REDISTRIBUTION
     You may not redistribute, publish, host, mirror, archive, or share any
     part of this repository without explicit written permission from
     Pedro Neiva. This applies to all hosting platforms, including GitHub,
     GitLab, Bitbucket, Gitea, Codeberg, and any cloud or file-sharing service.

  3. NO COMMERCIAL USE
     Commercial use of any material from this repository is strictly
     prohibited. This includes using implementations as the basis for
     commercial products, services, or consulting deliverables.

  4. NO CLAIMING OWNERSHIP
     You may not claim authorship or ownership of any code, documentation,
     architecture, or concept found in this repository.

  5. INTENTIONALLY MODIFIED & CONCEPTUAL CODE
     Certain scripts, algorithms, and security proofs-of-concept contain
     deliberate errors, missing logic, or modified structures. This is done
     purposely to demonstrate theoretical concepts while preventing blind
     copy-pasting. Running copied code without full comprehension will fail.

  6. 42 SCHOOL STUDENTS
     Copying any part of this code for submission at 42 School or any of
     its campuses worldwide constitutes plagiarism and a violation of the
     42 Peer-to-Peer integrity system.

  7. OTHER ACADEMIC INSTITUTIONS
     The same prohibition applies to MIT OpenCourseWare, Harvard CS50,
     Stanford, Princeton, Berkeley, Carnegie Mellon, Oxford, ETH Zurich,
     EPFL, or any other academic challenge, course, or institution worldwide.

  8. SECURITY CONTENT
     Content in 08-cybersecurity-and-cryptography/, 04-laboratory/,
     06-challenges/02-ctf-and-wargames/, and 07-chaos/ demonstrates
     vulnerability exploitation, reverse engineering, malware analysis,
     and adversarial techniques for strictly educational and research
     purposes within controlled academic contexts. Misuse of any content
     in these domains for malicious, illegal, or unauthorized purposes
     is the sole legal and ethical responsibility of the actor.

